    "body": "This PR partially addresses the subtree lint scope inconsistencies discussed in #34928.\n\nThe Python shell linters, `lint-shell.py` and `lint-shell-locale.py`, now use `SHARED_EXCLUDED_SUBTREES` instead of maintaining hardcoded subtree exclusions.\n\nThis also removes the overly broad regex in `lint-shell.py` while preserving the current set of excluded shell scripts.\n\nThe explicit per-linter subtree opt-ins discussed in #34928 are not implemented in this PR. This change focuses on consolidating the existing exclusions without modifying the current lint scope.\n\nCompared the original exclusion logic against the shared subtree list for all 61 tracked `.sh` files:\n\n| Linter | Before excluded | After excluded |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `lint-shell.py` | 10 | 10 |\n| `lint-shell-locale.py` | 10 | 10 |\n\nBoth linters preserve their existing `.sh` file exclusion scope.\n\nThe following checks also passed:\n\n- `./ci/lint.py`\n- `./ci/lint.py --lint=all_python_linters`\n- `./ci/lint.py --lint=py_lint`\n\nRelated to #34928.\n",
